# 1e999 overflows float; strtof flags it with ERANGE as a side effect but
# still returns a usable (infinite) value, so GMANRIBTokenize::parseNum
# returns a REAL token rather than throwing. parseNum's own integer branch
# no longer reads errno at all -- it bounds the parsed long directly
# against RtInt's range -- so this fixture no longer exercises a distinct
# code path from clipping_literal_overflow.rib's; retained as fixture data
# only, not wired into an assertion.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 1e999
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
Sides 4
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
